      "before": "kpk1-l20-c2-e01",
      "title": {
        "en": "W Krakowie, do Krakowa"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "For most cities and countries, and many regions and buildings, *gdzie?* takes *w* and the locative, and *dokąd?* takes *do* and the genitive: *jestem w Krakowie, jadę do Krakowa*. The same goes for *w Polsce, do Polski* and *w parku, do parku*. Some countries are plural: *w Niemczech, do Niemiec; w Czechach, do Czech*. Some places take *na* instead, like *na dworcu* and *na Mazurach*: they come in the next sets."
      },
      "table": {
        "title": {
          "en": "Miasto, kraj, budynek"
        },
